          <div class="alpha-row">
            <input type="range" id="alpha" name="alpha" min="0.50" max="0.95" step="0.05" value="0.85">
            <output id="alpha-value" class="alpha-value" for="alpha">0.85</output>
          </div>
          <p class="hint">1 - alpha is the restart probability. Validation sweeps 0.50, 0.70, 0.85 and 0.95.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label for="method">Method</label>
          <select id="method" name="method">
            <option value="popularity">popularity</option>
            <option value="pagerank">pagerank</option>
            <option value="ppr">ppr</option>
            <option value="mf">mf</option>
          </select>
          <p class="hint">Popularity counts distinct users with a positive training rating; pagerank uses a uniform restart; ppr restarts at the target user; mf reuses the previous matrix-factorization model.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="control">
          <label for="user-select">Target user (recommendations)</label>
