const notes = [
"HW6 week6 retains the existing data.js per-user chronological 80/10/10 split: 79619 training, 9596 validation, 10785 test ratings; preserve this source and avoid duplicate data-export files.",
"HW6 training graph has 943 user nodes, 1611 training movie nodes and 45602 binary undirected positive pairs from ratings >=4; retain zero-degree nodes and treat missing ratings as unobserved.",
"HW6 validation PPR sweep over 846 users selects alpha=0.50; Recall@10 values for 0.50/0.70/0.85/0.95 are 0.114483159132/0.104796950764/0.090020771553/0.073750303879 and match an independent float64 stationary solution.",
"TensorFlow.js WebGL asynchronous tensor data() stalled in the local IAB; batched PPR uses dataSync() and yields between iteration groups and batches.",
"Float32 bipartite PPR at alpha=0.95 could oscillate above 1e-6 until the iteration cap; enforce the exact partition mass (1 + alpha*(-alpha)^t)/(1+alpha) as a rounding correction while preserving p0=v, the restart equation, tolerance and cap.",
"HW6 Run tests now awaits batched PPR verification directly; verification refreshes a previously pending log and records actual failures; all 20 checks pass including 12 batch-versus-single user/alpha fixtures and tensor cleanup.",
"HW6 graph clicks select the clicked user as the PPR restart seed and recenter the ego view; the recommendation target remains independent and clicking the already selected seed is a no-op.",
"User requested the training/computation status immediately below Controls and the Run tests button inside Self-checks.",
"User requested two UI tabs: Main operations & recommendations contains every operation, evaluation, test and export button; Study fixture contains its own alpha, restart, Step and Reset controls.",
"HW6 main and fixture tabs use separate SVG, legend, convergence targets and alpha state; preserve results and fixture progress on switching, cache drawings per SVG for resizing and give SVG arrow markers unique IDs."
